# ==============================================================================
# Example 52: Saccharomyces cerevisiae S288C — Baker's Yeast
# ==============================================================================
#
# Organism: Saccharomyces cerevisiae S288C (model eukaryote)
# Genome: NCBI RefSeq NC_001133.9 (12,157,105 bp, 16 chromosomes)
# Environment: Synthetic complete medium, 30°C, aerobic
#
# S. cerevisiae is the premier model for eukaryotic cell biology, with
# extensive GEM support (iMM904, Szappanos et al. 2011). Its metabolism
# includes the Crabtree effect (overflow ethanol production at high glucose)
# and fermentative/respiratory diauxic shift.
#
# Life activities modeled:
#   1. Glycolysis — TDH3: glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase
#   2. Glycolysis — PGK1: phosphoglycerate kinase
#   3. Pyruvate metabolism — PDC1: pyruvate decarboxylase
#   4. TCA cycle — CIT1: citrate synthase (mitochondrial)
#
# Gene sequences: real S. cerevisiae S288C proteins from NCBI Protein
# database, back-translated to codon-optimized DNA.
#
# Growth medium: glucose minimal (10 mmol/L glucose)
# Expected growth rate: ~0.56 h^-1 (Koerkamp et al. 2012, G3 2:1561)
# ==============================================================================

#gem organism=s_cerevisiae medium=glucose_minimal use_database=true include_spontaneous=true gapfill=true dynamic=true duration=24.0 dt=0.05 expression=true target_organism=Saccharomyces_cerevisiae_S288C

